# Decisions — what · why · rejected alternative · decided by
D1 · Interface the graders call = REST route handlers (§7) + src/lib/billing.ts + PostgREST/Storage + webhook · the brief names all four · server-actions-only API · brief
D2 · Error body `{ "error": "message" }`; order 401 → 404 (not visible) → 403 (role) → 400 → 409/422 · brief §6/§7 fix shape and codes · kit `{error:{code,message}}` · brief (conflict with kit, reported)
D3 · Money bigint sen in SQL, number in TS via one toSen() helper (throws if unsafe); MYR only with currency char(3) CHECK = 'MYR' · brief §8 says bigint; kit wants a currency CHECK · integer columns / no currency column · Marwan
D4 · billing.ts self-contained (imports nothing), holds the single half-up rounding function; money.ts re-exports it · graders import billing.ts directly and it must be pure · rounding in money.ts imported by billing.ts · Marwan
D5 · "Today in Malaysia" = UTC instant + 8 h, date part; SQL twin `(p_as_of at time zone 'Asia/Kuala_Lumpur')::date`; overdue grace 0 · MYT has no DST; brief R17 boundary is 16:00Z · Intl.DateTimeFormat per call; 7-day grace (only in Part B code) · Marwan
D6 · receivedAt input must carry an offset or Z (else 400); instants output as `…+08:00` · brief: instants are ISO 8601 with an offset · naive strings read as MYT · Marwan
D7 · Lock the lease row FOR UPDATE first in every money write (record/approve/reject/void/bill create/settle); webhook locks bill → lease · cap and allocation are lease-wide; one fixed order prevents deadlocks · SERIALIZABLE + retry, advisory locks · Marwan
D8 · Money writes are plpgsql functions in `private`, called by server code (Prisma as postgres) after requireRole; no grants to anon/authenticated · one transaction per operation, not reachable through PostgREST · Prisma-only TS transactions · Marwan
D9 · Manual payment idempotency: OPTIONAL `Idempotency-Key` header (uuid), UNIQUE (org_id, idempotency_key), replay → original, other payload → 409 · brief body has no key, so requiring one would 400 every grader call · kit rule "required uuid" · Marwan
D10 · Webhook dedupe = bill state machine under bill FOR UPDATE + partial UNIQUE (payments.gateway_bill_id); no webhook_events table, no 5-minute replay window · brief: "a bill creates at most one payment, ever"; simulator makes a new transaction_id each run; no signed timestamp · dedupe on (provider,event_id)/transaction_id; replay window · Marwan
D11 · Webhook state follows the `paid` flag; amount compared with the bill's stored amount_sen; 422 on mismatch even though money is "captured" · brief table R34 · kit "never reject captured money" · brief
D12 · Payments never deleted: trigger blocks DELETE and allows only pending→approved/rejected and approved→voided status updates; other columns immutable · brief changes status in place · kit "voids are new rows" · Marwan
D13 · Cap = Σinvoices − Σallocations − Σpending; approve re-check = Σinvoices − Σallocations (pending ignored); bill amount due ignores pending · brief wording R22/R23/R30 · subtract other pending at approval · Marwan
D14 · Void leaves other payments' unapplied_sen untouched (no auto re-allocation) · brief: "Other payments' allocations do not change" · re-apply credit to reopened invoices · Marwan
D15 · Cross-org unitId/tenantId in POST /api/leases body → 404 · brief: records in another org get 404, never reveal existence · 400/422 · Marwan
D16 · Lease overlap = EXCLUDE USING gist (unit_id =, daterange(start,end,'[]') &&) → 23P01 → 409 · race-proof in the DB · SELECT-then-INSERT check · Marwan
D17 · Tenants map via tenants.user_id UNIQUE(org_id,user_id); staff/manager via memberships UNIQUE(user_id) · brief §6 + "exactly one organization" · UNIQUE(user_id, org_id) · Marwan
D18 · Prisma connects as postgres (owner, bypasses RLS); every service does requireRole + scopes by checked org_id · brief Part B states this setup · per-request JWT claims to apply RLS to Prisma · Marwan
D19 · audit_log append-only via BEFORE UPDATE/DELETE row trigger + BEFORE TRUNCATE trigger (applies to owner and service_role) · brief R43 · revoke-only (owner bypasses grants) · Marwan
D20 · Seed = `npm run seed` → tsx scripts/seed.ts using Admin API + the real services; supabase/seed.sql empty · brief: "through your normal code paths" · seed.sql inserts · brief (conflict with kit, reported)
D21 · Env file `.env.local` (brief); prisma7.config.ts + seed load `.env.local` then `.env` via dotenv `config({ path: ['.env.local', '.env'] })` · grader runs `cp .env.example .env.local` · `.env` · brief (conflict with kit)
D22 · Slip storage: bucket payment-slips private, 5 MiB, jpeg/png/pdf; path `<org_id>/<lease_id>/<uuid>.<ext>`; staff/manager INSERT+SELECT own org folder; server verifies storage.objects row in caller org, deletes on failure; UNIQUE(slip_path); slip on cash → 400 · brief §4/§6 · server-side upload via our API · Marwan
D23 · Submitted DECISIONS.md = Part C answers first, then this log; transcripts in app/ai-logs/ · brief §Part C + Submission · kit log only / session-logs/ · Marwan
D24 · Seed password RentDemo#2026 shared by all accounts (SEED_PASSWORD in .env.example) · brief asks for one password · — · Marwan
D25 · Collections report returns every month in [from, to] via generate_series over MYT months, left-joined to approved payments grouped by (received_at at time zone 'Asia/Kuala_Lumpur') month · brief example [300000, 0, 200000] includes the empty month · GROUP BY only (drops empty months) · Marwan
D26 · The UI always sends receivedAt with an explicit +08:00 offset (datetime-local input interpreted as MYT, never the browser zone) · server rejects naive instants (D6) · new Date(input).toISOString() in the browser zone · Marwan
D27 · cacheComponents: false in next.config.ts · create-next-app 16 sets true, which fails next build on pages that read cookies · keep true · kit rule (Marwan, pre-exam)
D28 · UI mutations call the REST routes with fetch (cookie session); server components read through the same services; no separate server actions · one code path, which the hidden tests exercise · server actions duplicating each route · pending
D29 · Test fixtures (orgs/users created by tests) are not deleted: audit_log and payments are append-only by design, so fixture orgs stay until the next db reset; tests use fresh random orgs so they never collide · brief R25/R43 forbid deleting them · per-test cleanup (impossible without breaking append-only) · pending
D30 · backend-engineer may run ../scripts/db-reset.sh (exclusive lock) only to test npm run seed on a fresh DB, on the lead's order · the seed must be proven on a fresh DB and it lives in the backend lane · lead runs every seed check · pending
# REFERENCE — verified on this machine on 2026-10-24
Node v20.20.1, npm 10.8.2, Docker 29.1.3. Working project: /home/electronica-care/ezy-prep/dryrun/app
Versions that worked: Next 16.4.3, React 19.3.0, Prisma 7.10.1, @prisma/client 7.10.1 (+ @prisma/adapter-pg 7.10.1, pg), @supabase/ssr 0.12.7, @supabase/supabase-js 2.118.0, supabase CLI 2.122.0, Vitest 4.1.12, shadcn 4.22.1 (style base-nova), Tailwind 4.3.3, ESLint 9.39.5, TS 5.9.3.
Prisma schemas setting that db pull accepted: `schemas = ["auth", "public"]` (public-only FAILS with P4002 because memberships.user_id -> auth.users).

## Setup commands that worked, in order
```bash
npx --yes create-next-app@16 app --ts --app --src-dir --tailwind --eslint --no-turbopack --import-alias "@/*" --use-npm --yes
cd app
npx supabase@2.122.0 init && sed -i 's/^project_id = "app"/project_id = "<name>"/' supabase/config.toml
npx supabase@2.122.0 start            # run in background; continue with installs meanwhile
echo 'node-options=--experimental-websocket' > .npmrc     # GOTCHA 1, do before anything runs supabase-js
npm i @prisma/client@7.10.1 @prisma/adapter-pg@7.10.1 pg @supabase/ssr @supabase/supabase-js
npm i -D prisma@7.10.1 @types/pg dotenv
npm i -D vitest@4 --legacy-peer-deps                     # GOTCHA 2 + 3
npx prisma init --datasource-provider postgresql         # writes prisma7.config.ts, prisma/schema.prisma, .env
npx --yes shadcn@latest init -y -d                       # also creates components/ui/button.tsx
npx shadcn@latest add button -y
npm pkg set scripts.postinstall="prisma generate" scripts.test="vitest run" scripts.typecheck="tsc --noEmit"
# write .env from supabase (overwrite the prisma placeholder):
eval "$(npx supabase status -o env 2>/dev/null | grep -E '^(API_URL|ANON_KEY|SERVICE_ROLE_KEY|DB_URL)=')"
printf 'NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=%s\nNEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=%s\nSUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=%s\nDATABASE_URL=%s\n' "$API_URL" "$ANON_KEY" "$SERVICE_ROLE_KEY" "$DB_URL" > .env
# add migration supabase/migrations/20261024000001_init.sql + supabase/seed.sql, then:
npx supabase db reset                 # if it says DbSetupError "exit 1" right after start: just rerun
# add schemas = ["auth","public"] to datasource, then:
npx prisma db pull && npx prisma generate
npx tsc --noEmit && npx eslint . --max-warnings=0 && npm run build
for tz in UTC Asia/Dubai America/New_York; do TZ=$tz npx vitest run; done
npx supabase stop
```
`supabase status -o env` names: API_URL (http://127.0.0.1:54321), REST_URL, DB_URL (…:54322/postgres), STUDIO_URL (:54323), MAILPIT_URL (:54324), ANON_KEY, SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, PUBLISHABLE_KEY (sb_publishable_…), SECRET_KEY (sb_secret_…), JWT_SECRET.

## Timing (this machine, cold caches)
create-next-app ~7 min (npm install), supabase start first time ~19 min (image pulls; ~1 min once images cached), npm installs ~5 min, shadcn ~40 s. Steps 1–6 wall-clock ≈ 32 min. **Start `supabase start` in background first**; images are now cached on this machine.

## Gotchas + fixes
1. **supabase-js 2.118 on Node 20 throws `Node.js detected but native WebSocket not found`** at createClient (node scripts, vitest). Fix: `.npmrc` with `node-options=--experimental-websocket` (applies to npm run / npx), or `node --experimental-websocket script.mjs`. The Next server (dev/start) worked without it.
2. **vitest 5 requires Node >=22** → use `vitest@4` (4.1.12).
3. `npm i -D vitest` fails with `Cannot read properties of null (reading 'edgesOut')` (npm 10.8.2 bug on optional peer jsdom→canvas). Fix: `--legacy-peer-deps` (once; later plain `npm i` works).
4. **`npm i prisma` installs 8.0.0-rc.27** (npm `latest` tag is an RC) while @prisma/client latest is 7.10.1. Pin both: `prisma@7.10.1 @prisma/client@7.10.1`.
5. Prisma 7: no `url` in schema.prisma; URL lives in config; client needs driver adapter (`@prisma/adapter-pg`); generator `prisma-client` with output `../src/generated/prisma`, import from `@/generated/prisma/client`. `prisma init` writes **prisma7.config.ts** (legacy `prisma.config.ts` is still accepted). It also drops agent skill dirs (.agents/.claude/.windsurf, skills-lock.json) — gitignored them.
6. `prisma db pull` with default (public only): P4002 cross-schema reference to auth.users → `schemas = ["auth","public"]` (pulls ~27 auth models + enums; fine). Models get `@@schema("public")`.
7. First `supabase db reset` right after start failed `DbSetupError: error running container: exit 1`; rerun succeeded.
8. vitest.config: `import { loadEnvConfig } from "@next/env"` fails in .mts (CJS) → `import nextEnv from "@next/env"; nextEnv.loadEnvConfig(process.cwd())`. Use `vitest.config.mts` (a .ts config warns about ESM-as-CJS).
9. Top-level await in a tsx script: name it `.mts` (`npx --yes tsx scripts/prisma-check.mts`).
10. create-next-app 16 sets `cacheComponents: true` in next.config.ts; /api/me with cookies() still built as dynamic (ƒ) — no change needed. AGENTS.md says read node_modules/next/dist/docs/.
11. ESLint: Next 16 flat config (`eslint.config.mjs`, defineConfig + globalIgnores) passed `--max-warnings=0` unchanged; added `"src/generated/**"` to globalIgnores (not strictly needed).
12. create-next-app `.gitignore` has `.env*` (would ignore .env.example) → replace with `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env*.local`, `!.env.example`; check `git ls-files .env.example`.
13. `postinstall: prisma generate` verified to succeed with no `.env` and no DATABASE_URL.
14. Kit says `vitest.config.ts`: a `.ts` config works but prints an ESM-as-CJS warning; `.mts` is clean (needs the default-import fix in 8).
15. Don't `pkill -f 'next start'` from a shell whose command line contains that string — kills itself. Kill by pid from `ss -ltnp | grep :3000`.

## Migration 0001 essentials (RLS on, anon locked out)
```sql
create table public.orgs (id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(), name text not null, created_at timestamptz not null default now());
create table public.memberships (id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(),
  user_id uuid not null references auth.users(id) on delete cascade,
  org_id uuid not null references public.orgs(id) on delete cascade,
  role text not null check (role in ('manager','staff','tenant')),
  created_at timestamptz not null default now(), unique (user_id, org_id));
alter table public.orgs enable row level security;
alter table public.memberships enable row level security;
revoke all on all tables in schema public from anon;
revoke all on all sequences in schema public from anon;
revoke all on all functions in schema public from anon;
alter default privileges in schema public revoke all on tables from anon;
alter default privileges in schema public revoke all on sequences from anon;
alter default privileges in schema public revoke all on functions from anon;
-- + private.has_role below, then:
create policy "memberships: read own" on public.memberships for select to authenticated using (user_id = (select auth.uid()));
create policy "orgs: members read" on public.orgs for select to authenticated using (private.has_role(id, array['manager','staff','tenant']));
```
